House","dish/wolfie-cohen-s-rascal-house"]]}]},"dish/alplermagronen":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/alplermagronen","n":"Älplermagronen","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Swiss cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Älplermagronen, also spelled Älplermakkaronen, is a dish from the Alpine regions of Switzerland, consisting of pasta, potatoes, cream, cheese, and onions. The name is made up of \"Älpler\" as a designation for the Alpine herder and \"Magronen\", which was taken as a loan word from the Italian word maccheroni."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-alplermagronen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%84lplermagronen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Swiss cuisine","cuisine/swiss-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Noodles","ingredient/noodles"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Helvetic Kitchen","ref":"site/helvetickitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"helvetickitchen.com","note":"Andie Pilot's blog of Swiss home cooking and baking, with notes on Swiss cookbooks.","url":"https://www.helvetickitchen.com/recipes/retrospective","suggested":true},{"name":"Cuisine Helvetica","ref":"site/cuisinehelvetica-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cuisinehelvetica.com","note":"Heddi Nieuwsma's Swiss recipes and food culture from her life in Switzerland.","url":"https://cuisinehelvetica.com/swiss-recipes","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Swiss cuisine","links":[["Basler Läckerli","dish/basler-lackerli"],["Birnbrot","dish/birnbrot"],["Bündnerfleisch","dish/bundnerfleisch"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Carac (pastry)","dish/carac-pastry"],["Cervelat","dish/cervelat"],["Cholera (food)","dish/cholera-food"],["Egg puffs and soup pearls","dish/egg-puffs-and-soup-pearls"],["Landjäger","dish/landjager"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Raclette","dish/raclette"],["R